# Five berths of six are taken and a scout moves in, which is the sixth.
#
# **Every number is on the page.** A territory provides six; territory-2 holds two transports at
# two and a scout at one, which is five; the scout arriving makes six.

{test name:a-scout-moves-where-there-is-a-berth-to-spare}

{given}
{provides kind:13 what:1 quantity:6}
{consumes kind:28 what:1 quantity:1}
{consumes kind:35 what:1 quantity:2}
{territory id:1}
{territory id:2}
{adjacency id:1 from:1 to:2}
{scout where:1 quantity:1}
{transport where:2 quantity:2}
{scout where:2 quantity:1}

{when}
{move what:28 from:1 to:2}

{then}
{provides kind:13 what:1 quantity:6}
{consumes kind:28 what:1 quantity:1}
{consumes kind:35 what:1 quantity:2}
{territory id:1}
{territory id:2}
{adjacency id:1 from:1 to:2}
{transport where:2 quantity:2}
{scout where:2 quantity:2}
